# text = In terms of the professional society of human factors engineers, however, the majority of the money comes from military sources (even for disabled tech research), and although the society newsletter occasionally prints letters with political/social criticism (e.g. protesting against the "custer's revenge" video game), they are usually concerned more with trying to get conservative interests (industry-military) interested in hiring human factors engineers, and tend to shy away from any taint of social critique.
