# text = Donna's lecture was pitched to getting the Santa Cruz feminist/lit crit crowd more interested in science, it was a great success with her audience (afterwards African-American lit maven bell hooks said in an astonished voice "hey, this is the same thing we're trying to do in Black women's literature!") but was a catastrophe for my physicist, who said "typical view of science-is-male-domination."
